sipc, mailbox: drop the "base_addr" attributes that can never be read

Neither show nor store, created on platform devices that are never registered: two warnings each at boot, about
ten seconds in all on the 5.4 console (docs/FINDINGS.md 31g).

diff -ru a/drivers/soc/sprd/modem/sipc/sblock.c b/drivers/soc/sprd/modem/sipc/sblock.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sprd/modem/sipc/sblock.c	2026-09-27 16:21:13
+++ b/drivers/soc/sprd/modem/sipc/sblock.c	2026-09-27 16:21:28
@@ -2184,7 +2184,6 @@
 	.release = single_release,
 };
 
-static DEVICE_ATTR(base_addr, 0440, NULL, NULL);
 
 int sblock_init_debug(void)
 {
@@ -2218,7 +2217,8 @@
 	sblock_dev->sys_dev = device_create(sblock_class, NULL,
 				       dev_no,
 				       sblock_dev, "sipc_sblock");
-	device_create_file(&sblock_dev->pdev.dev, &dev_attr_base_addr);
+	/* MU300: the vendor also created a "base_addr" attribute here: with neither show nor store, on a device that
+	 * is never registered - it could never be read, and each one warned twice (about a second of boot each) */
 
 	return 0;
 
